      "writtenOn": "2018-09-03T05:51:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So IIUC, we send a bunch of\n\n{ EC_CMD_FP_TEMPLATE, chunk size, nonce\u003ddon\u0027t care, salt\u003ddon\u0027t care, tag\u003ddon\u0027t care, data\u003dtemplate chunk }\n\nand then:\n\n{ EC_CMD_FP_TEMPLATE, FP_TEMPLATE_COMMIT | chunk size, nonce, salt, tag, data }\n\nSending nonce/salt/tag with every chunk seems wasteful, maybe we should have something like:\n\nunion {\n  struct {\n    uint8_t nonce[FP_CONTEXT_NONCE_BYTES];\n    uint8_t salt[FP_CONTEXT_SALT_BYTES];\n    uint8_t tag[FP_CONTEXT_TAG_BYTES];\n  } encryption_metadata;\n  uint8_t data[];\n}\n\nAnd not allow data to be sent with the metadata?",
